From c6266851a9c7d96a347911700a0ea0335a9e6361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TB378FC Maintainer <maintainer@tb378fc.local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:06:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform: tb378fc: fix schedutil 4.32 GHz boost, nt36536, and
 DTS warnings

1. cpufreq/schedutil: map utilization against min(cpuinfo.max_freq,
   policy->max) when policy->boost_enabled is active and policy->max
   exceeds sustained arch_scale_freq_ref, unlocking 4.20/4.32 GHz SCMI
   Boost OPPs on CPU6-7 under schedutil + EAS + uclamp without shifting
   non-boost capacity ratios. Reset cpuinfo.max_freq in
   cpufreq_boost_set_sw() so disabling boost clamps policy limits back
   to sustained frequency cleanly.
2. Input: nt36536: disable NVT_DEBUG=1 pr_err flood (downgrade NVT_LOG
   to pr_debug) and cache parsed firmware + header map in RAM across
   panel wake cycles to avoid repeated filesystem reads and checksums.
3. Bluetooth: btqca: use firmware_request_nowarn() when probing optional
   WCN7860 candidate filenames before Lenovo brhbtfw*.tlv fallback.
4. power: supply: qcom_battmgr: set QCOM_BATTMGR_QUIRK_NO_CHARGE_CONTROL
   on lenovo,tb378fc-pmic-glink where Android PMIC GLINK does not
   implement Windows-on-Arm opcode 0x48 charge thresholds.
5. DTS & audio/camera polish: add wcd939x MBHC voltage thresholds and
   lpass_vamacro dmic-sample-rate to sm8750-lenovo-tb378fc.dts,
   downgrade intentional SoundWire DT port-count override log to
   dev_dbg, and use dev_err_probe() for deferred CAMSS CSIPHY init.

6. usb/dp/coresight: expose DWC3 Type-C mode-switch on TB378FC (&usb) so
   4-lane DisplayPort (Pin Assignment C/E, e.g. 5120x2880) switches DWC3
   to UTMI clock before QMP powers down pipe_clk, preventing xHCI/DWC3
   hangs and watchdog SoC resets on unplug; guard msm_dp_audio_shutdown()
   against unclocked MMIO writes after DP power-off; and disable unused
   CoreSight trace NOC (tn@109ab000).
7. Input: nt36536: defer panel-follower firmware load via delayed_work
   with firmware_request_nowarn() until rootfs /lib/firmware/novatek/
   tb378fc.bin mounts, fixing cold-boot dead touch without screen off/on.

Signed-off-by: TB378FC Maintainer <maintainer@tb378fc.local>
---
